# ArduCopter frame for the Aero Sense hexacopter, loaded after copter.parm (simulation.launch.py).
# Hexa X: motor order and spin in aero_sense_description/render.py HEXA_X.
FRAME_CLASS 2
FRAME_TYPE 1
# Fly on EKF3, fed by the GPS, compass, baro and IMU, as the real drone does. The Gazebo plugin's
# <no_time_sync> makes SITL default this to 10, its perfect simulated state: flown that way, the
# drone knew where it was without any sensor, and losing GPS changed nothing.
AHRS_EKF_TYPE 3
# EKF source set 3: no horizontal position, baro height, compass yaw. drone_interface switches to it
# when GPS is lost and OpenVINS cannot take over: left on set 1, the EKF took the jammer's fake
# fixes and flew the drone after them. Without a position, the EKF failsafe lands where it is.
EK3_SRC3_POSXY 0
EK3_SRC3_VELXY 0
EK3_SRC3_POSZ 1
EK3_SRC3_VELZ 0
EK3_SRC3_YAW 1

# Obstacle avoidance from the four TF rangefinders (config/sensors.yaml), which drone_interface
# sends as MAVLink DISTANCE_SENSOR. PRX1_TYPE 2 is the MAVLink proximity backend. ArduPilot then
# reports the proximity sensor healthy and stops the drone short in the pilot's modes, but
# neither simple avoidance nor BendyRuler touches the GUIDED position targets the mission flies
# (docs/VERIFICATION.md): the drone flew into a wall its own beam was reading. These are set so
# the autopilot has the obstacles too; what actually stops the drone is the guard in obstacle.py.
PRX1_TYPE 2
PRX1_ORIENT 0
AVOID_ENABLE 2
AVOID_MARGIN 3
AVOID_BEHAVE 0
OA_TYPE 1
OA_MARGIN_MAX 3
OA_BR_LOOKAHEAD 8

# ArduPilot's own DDS client, off: this stack talks MAVLink, there is no micro-ROS agent for it
# to find, and its "DDS: No ping response, exiting" was the last thing it said before every
# unrelated timeout, which sent us looking for a fault in the wrong place.
DDS_ENABLE 0
